  "preamble": "The loss or elision of the lateral consonant /l/, often in syllable-final position or in specific clusters. In Southern Tsakonian, [l] was deleted before back and central vowels (λόγος > όγο), while Northern Tsakonian keeps it. In Galician-Portuguese single intervocalic l was lost (Latin dolōrem > door > dor 'pain', volāre > voar 'to fly').",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, L-dropping",
